WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would imagine,
based on not liking

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:06.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
the crowds leaving,
the "SNL" New Orleans

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mardi Gras Special
must have been

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.009 line:92%
incredibly traumatic, as well,

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
because,
for those who don't know,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the second season
of "SNL."

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne decided to bring the cas
down to do a live show,

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:20.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
live two-hour special,
at Mardi Gras,

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I believe
eliminated the decision

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
to ever try to do anything
like that ever again,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.828 line:92%
based on how it went down.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.263 line:92%
-It was such a good idea.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:36.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- the planning that wa
involved was so meticulous

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:40.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, every --
every minute was counted for

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had -- not.
I was --

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:45.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Did you think it was

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bad idea
when you first heard it?

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:49.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I thought
it would be really fun,

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause, you know,
we're with a group,

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we would be well taken
care of and protected.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:58.992 size:84% position:42% line:92%
But it wasn't that way.

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was doing
the color commentary

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.630 line:92%
for the parade with Buck Henry

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.533
So, Buck and I didn't have any
rehearsal to do during the wee

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there was
no parade during the week,

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we just played,
and we just sort of

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:12.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
wandered around the street
during Mardi Gras.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:17.977
Henry Winkler was in town, and
at that time, the Fonz was huge.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And people thought

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Jack Lemon was in town,
and they thought

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.384
that Buck was Jack Lemon,
so they'd come up and say,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:27.620 size:88% position:44%
"Mr. Lemon, Mr. Lemon,
have you seen the Fonz?"

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Buck would go,
"Charles Street.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
Charles Street,
about 10 minutes ago."

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.793 line:92%
So we just had a great time.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile, Gilda and Laraine
and Dan and John

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.366 size:81% position:41%
are out doing sketches
or rehearsing sketches

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.869 line:92%
in the middle of Mardi Gras,

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's
no police protection.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:50.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
So people are storming Gilda
They're accosting her.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.246 line:92%
They're throwing Laraine around.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it was just --
It was horrible.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just horrible.
But then, the day of the parad

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
happens and the day
of the show happens,

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.956 line:92%
and Randy Newman opens the show.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's in a --
the convention center,

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.293 line:92%
and there's an audience there.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't know who else
is doing the show.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then,
they cut to the parade,

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's Buck and me,
and we're sta-- we're sittin

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a platform
above the parade route,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:19.405
and there are 15,000 peopl
who are really plastered,

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
shouting our names
and throwing bottles

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.009 line:92%
and doubloons in our faces

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:23.877 line:92%
And we're sitting there going,

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:26.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, the parade
should be here any minute.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.282
We think it's gonna be great
and we heard that they were --

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:33.820
oh! -- lots of people --
ow! -- lots of people here

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lots of people here.
Buck, what do you think?

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lots of people."
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:41.161 size:81% position:41%
It sounds horrifying.
-It was so horrifying.

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:44.264
And we were dodging doubloon
and all this kind of stuff

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there was a writer,
a sound guy,

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.336 size:84% position:42% line:92%
a cameraman, and a P.A.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's what we had
up in this little platform

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:57.844 size:88% position:44%
So, at the parade route,
there was an accident.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I think
it was a fatal accident,

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:05.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
so the parade never happened
but...

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:06.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
-...it did in our minds.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we described the parade
that we saw

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
coming down the street,
dodging doubloons and bottles.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
The show ended,
and people are climbing up

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:23.903 line:92%
onto the platform to get at us

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
-And -- yeah.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:28.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the P.A. is stomping
on their fingers,

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.709 size:84% position:42% line:92%
trying to pry them off.

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
And somebody screams,
"We need police protection,"

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.382 line:92%
and somebody screamed back

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
"There are no policemen
available!"

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Buck and I are going -
[ Shuddering ]

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause there are people
all around.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.758 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We couldn't get down.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:49.429
They send two detectives,
two retired detectives,

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
guys in their 60s,
wearing trench coats,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
a little bit of a beer belly

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
They come, and they said,
"Okay, okay, come on, come on,

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
come on down, come on down
come on down."

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're climbing off
the scaffolding, climbing down

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
They grab us
in a fireman's hold,

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.579 line:92%
throw us over their shoulders.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:10.183
We're marching through the crowd
of 20,000 people.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm wailing,
I'm crying so hard.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:14.654 line:92%
Just the release of tensio

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I was saved
by these guys.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:20.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buck, I think,
was in the same boat.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when they went
to drop us to, you know,

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
to let us down and say,
"Okay, that's it,"

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:25.898 line:92%
we didn't want to let go.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, no, I'm sorry.
I'll die if I let go of you.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will die."
But they pried my little hands

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
off of his trench coat
and sent me off on my way.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so happy you went through
that so I never have to.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:43.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Ah, well,
it was my pleasure, Seth.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.019 line:92%
-Was -- I always regretted

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:49.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I never got a chance
to meet Buck Henry.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.790 line:92%
Was he one of your favorites

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
He was my all-time favorite.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:54.794 line:92%
Buck and I worked together

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.363
oh, for a long time after
"Saturday Night Live."

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:03.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did an NPR show
for 11 or 12 years

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:07.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Robert Krulwich
and Tony Hendra.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:11.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buck and me and Herb Sargent
was the producer.

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, you know,
we just hung out.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess once
you go through something

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.885 line:92%
like New Orleans together,

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're probably
just like forever...

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's true.
-Forever fused.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:26.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no, no, no,
we bonded, we bonded.

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:29.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:29.062 --> 00:05:29.796 line:92%
Congrats on the new show,

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's always
such a delight to see you.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.701 line:92%
-Good to see you, too, Seth.

